    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **273 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented sequential membership numbers for newly created owners, returned as the integer field `membershipNumber` in the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `membershipNumber` integer (int32) property to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerDto` (with `membershipNumber`) at build time, and MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a persistent `membershipNumber` field (`@Column(name = \"membership_number\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 In `saveOwner`, for new owners set `membershipNumber = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1` (one more than the current owner count). JPA auto-flush before the count query ensures each successive creation sees the previous one, so consecutive owners increment by exactly one.\n\n4. **DB schema (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`)** \u2014 Added a `membership_number` column to the `owners` table so the value persists and is read back on `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n5. **Seed data (`db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql`)** \u2014 The positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` seeds needed a value for the new column; gave the 10 seed owners membership numbers matching their id (1\u201310). The h2/postgres seeds use explicit column lists and were unaffected.\n\nThe new `Cp09Tests.coreMembershipNumberIsSequential` passes (creating two owners and confirming their membership numbers differ by exactly one), along with all pre-existing tests.",
